{
  "version": 3,
  "meta": {
    "name": "cable_route_weave_vision",
    "description": "Weave the cable from RGB-D alone. A placed third-person camera (1280x960 at 600 mm) is read once per crossing: SAM3 grounds the cable, TrackDLO orders its skeleton into a centreline, and later passes update that model rather than re-fitting it. The SUPPORT HAND takes the far end first -- a free cable translates rather than bends, so without an anchor the first crossing hauls the whole cable and the next has nothing to grasp. Then one crossing per pass: track, mate, take, carry, seat, release, back to the gate. The crossing loop re-fits the centreline before every station; a final re-fit runs after the last one, because `plug` has to grasp the rod's free END and the memory it read was two crossings stale -- measured, it reached to where the end had been at the opening frame, closed on nothing, and reported a delivery that never happened.",
    "composes": {
      "anchor_sg": "grasping-curve-point",
      "perceive_sg": "perceiving-functional-features",
      "release_sg": "executing-feature-mating"
    },
    "composes_note": "Subgraphs listed in `composes` run this graph's own scripts for the named skill, so they are labelled `generic`: graph-as-policy's SK1/SK2 contract reserves a bundle label for subgraphs that run that bundle's canonical scripts."
  },
